# OpenGamepadUI — the gamepad shell gamescope hosts. Local PKGBUILD (packages/opengamepadui/PKGBUILD).
#
# Was a prebuilt pin of upstream's aarch64 release tarball until 2026-10-02, when the first hardware
# boot (KONKR Pocket FIT, SM8650) showed v0.46.1 cannot run on these boards:
#
#   0001  upstream #542: HardwareManager reads /sys/devices/virtual/dmi/id/product_name, which does
#         not exist on a devicetree board (no SMBIOS from the ABL UEFI), and calls a method on the
#         null FileAccess -- a SIGSEGV in a release build, ~10s into every start, so the session
#         crash-loops behind a black panel. On ARM the name comes from the devicetree model
#         instead ("Unknown" if empty), as asked in review of upstream PR #559.
#   0002  upstream #540: Godot 4.7 added a native Control.custom_maximum_size, so the two install
#         dialogs that declare their own fail to compile, and game_launch_menu.gd (which depends on
#         them) never loads -- picking a game does nothing, on every platform.
#   0003  ours, for upstream: the performance menu showed TDP, thermal-limit and power-profile
#         controls for any integrated GPU. An SoC GPU (Adreno, via our PowerStation devfreq
#         backend) has none of them, so they appeared with a -1 range and wrote nowhere. Shown now
#         only when HardwareManager reports the capability.
#   0004  ours, for upstream: an app that exits before creating a window never left the running
#         list (its type stays unknown, and only X11/Wayland apps get the is_running() checks), so
#         a ROM whose emulator is not installed hung on the loading screen and the plugin's EXIT
#         hook never ran. While the type is unknown, mark the app stopped on the first failed
#         is_running() check (the reaper it tracks outlives every process of the app), ~1 s.
#   0005  ours, for upstream (to confirm with the authors first): a missing default performance
#         profile is created from the settings applied at that moment, which on a fresh install
#         is when the last game stops -- a game's CPU core count became the default and stayed
#         applied after it exited (HW, Pocket FIT, 2026-10-04). Save the startup settings as the
#         default of each profile state (docked = charging, undocked) that has none.
#   0006  ours, for upstream (branch feat/power-profiles-without-tdp): power profiles on a GPU
#         with no TDP. PowerStation's devfreq backend offers them (CPU + GPU governor pairs), but
#         the menu only showed the dropdown for a matched AMD APU, only in simple mode, and as
#         presets that also reset cores / GPU clocks; a mode toggle forced max-performance. For
#         a GPU without a TDP: dropdown in both modes, a choice applies alone, toggles keep it.
#         The dropdown sits above the Advanced Mode toggle (a profile sets CPU + GPU governors).
#   0007  ours, for upstream (branch fix/profile-key-app-id): a game's performance profile was saved
#         under a hash of its card NAME, so renaming a card lost it (QForge renames same-named ROM
#         cards, and a metadata scrape will rename them all). Keyed by provider + app id now (for
#         QForge ROMs, <system>/<file>); a profile saved under the name is still loaded.
#   0008  ours, for upstream: the home banner's god-rays shader (screen texture with mipmaps,
#         animated with TIME) and the focused card's god-rays + shine keep the whole UI redrawing
#         every frame, so low_processor_mode never idles: measured 47 ms of GPU per frame, the
#         Adreno 610 pinned at 1050 MHz and the shell at ~20 fps doing nothing (Air X, 2026-10-10;
#         hiding that one node took the shell to zero submits and the GPU to runtime-suspend).
#         A Settings > General "Animated Effects" toggle (general/animated_effects), off by
#         default, gates those shaders.
#
# The earlier 0006/0007 (plugin store URL as a project setting, set to "" for QForge) were dropped on
# 2026-10-06: with the store off, OGUI's first-start screen showed an empty catalog. QForge has no
# store of its own (its one plugin ships in the image and OTAs), so upstream's store stays.
#
# So the PKGBUILD keeps upstream's aarch64 engine binary, Rust core and reaper from the release
# tarball, and rebuilds only opengamepad-ui.pck from the tagged source plus these patches. Drop a
# patch when the release that fixes it is pinned.
#
# Fields (see packages/README.md):
#   name           pkgname (must match the PKGBUILD); also the work/ build-dir + repo entry
#   pkgbuild_local path (relative to this dir) to the checked-in PKGBUILD to build
#   pkgrel_suffix  numeric suffix appended to the PKGBUILD's pkgrel so pacman prefers our build
#   patches        files under patches/, applied in order right after prepare()'s first `cd`
name: opengamepadui
pkgbuild_local: PKGBUILD
pkgrel_suffix: 1
patches: 0001-hardware-manager-no-dmi.patch 0002-install-dialogs-rename-custom-maximum-size.patch 0003-performance-menu-hide-unsupported-controls.patch 0004-running-app-exit-before-window.patch 0005-performance-manager-save-default-profiles.patch 0006-performance-menu-power-profiles-without-tdp.patch 0007-performance-manager-profile-key-app-id.patch 0008-animated-effects-setting.patch
